cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the Epmej & Peumeu Monique decomposition in your research or embedded systems, please cite it using the metadata below."
type: software
title: "Epmej & Peumeu Monique + Heron: Deterministic O(1) Square Root Library for FPU-less Microcontrollers"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-07
authors:
  - family-names: "Djempe"
    given-names: "James"
    email: "epmejd@gmail.com"
    affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
abstract: >-
  A zero-dependency C mathematical library implementing the Epmej & Peumeu Monique
  decomposition combined with localized Heron (Babylonian) iterations for deterministic
  O(1) floating-point square root computation on FPU-less microcontrollers (ARM Cortex-M0/M0+,
  AVR ATmega328P, ESP8266). Achieves up to 72.6% CPU cycle and energy reduction while
  maintaining IEEE 754 double-precision accuracy (< 1.11e-16 relative error).
keywords:
  - "square root approximation"
  - "Epmej & Peumeu Monique property"
  - "Heron method"
  - "Babylonian method"
  - "embedded systems"
  - "FPU-less microcontrollers"
  - "numerical analysis"
  - "IEEE 754"
  - "low-power IoT"
license: "MIT"
preferred-citation:
  type: article
  authors:
    - family-names: "Djempe"
      given-names: "James"
      email: "epmejd@gmail.com"
      affiliation: "Independent Researcher"
  title: "An Analytical and Iterative Framework for Efficient Square Root Computation: The Epmej & Peumeu Monique Decomposition Combined with the Old-Babylonian Method"
  year: 2026
  month: 11
  abstract: >-
    Formalizes the Epmej & Peumeu Monique Property (Y = x^2 + m with x >= 1 and x >= 2|m|)
    to derive a deterministic initialization vector for the Heron method, eliminating native
    hardware SQRT calls and reducing energy consumption by 69.6% to 72.6% on FPU-less MCUs.
